    "text": "This program only delivers gifts that are already in reach of Lapland, so it scores low but never breaks a rule. For each gift whose location is within distance D of (0,0), it loads the gift and delivers it straight away while the sleigh stays at (0,0). No carrots, acceleration or floating are needed, so every output is valid. It does not plan any trips to gifts farther away.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){\n    long long T,D,W,G;\n    cin>>T>>D>>W>>G;\n    for(int i=0;i<W;i++){long long a,b;cin>>a>>b;}\n    vector<string> acts;\n    for(int i=0;i<G;i++){\n        string n;long long s,w,c,r;\n        cin>>n>>s>>w>>c>>r;\n        if(c*c+r*r<=D*D){\n            acts.push_back(\"LoadGift \"+n);\n            acts.push_back(\"DeliverGift \"+n);\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\",(int)acts.size());\n    for(auto&a:acts)printf(\"%s\\n\",a.c_str());\n}\n```",
